‎## 1. Directive
‎
‎A checklist against historical and present patterns is prudent — especially because it prevents the observation from becoming a story too early.
‎
‎**Rule:** Separate signal from story. Evidence before narrative.
‎
‎---
‎
‎## 2. Crossroads Pattern Checklist — 12 Stages
‎
‎For any ecosystem under stress, score each stage: **No Evidence / Weak Signal / Confirmed Evidence**
‎
‎| # | Stage | Signal | What to Measure | Status |
‎| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
‎| 01 | **Friction Appears** | Limits, reliability, pricing, access, performance degrade | Support tickets, latency, pricing changes, rate limits | [ ] |
‎| 02 | **Complaints Become Recurring** | Isolated dissatisfaction → visible theme | Frequency of same complaint across platforms, time | [ ] |
‎| 03 | **Evaluation Begins** | Users compare alternatives rather than merely complain | Search: "alternative to X", comparison posts, benchmarks | [ ] |
‎| 04 | **Experimentation Begins Quietly** | Users test competing systems | GitHub experiments, new tool usage, trial accounts | [ ] |
‎| 05 | **Work is Diversified** | People stop relying on one system for everything | Multi-tool workflows, portfolio approach | [ ] |
‎| 06 | **Portability Becomes Important** | Users ask whether workflows, knowledge, outputs can travel | Questions about export, migration, interoperability | [ ] |
‎| 07 | **Switching Costs Become Visible** | What actually prevents migration? | Lock-in analysis: data, identity, distribution, trust | [ ] |
‎| 08 | **Behaviour Precedes Declarations** | Usage patterns change before people announce migration | Usage data > declared intent. Quiet migration. | [ ] |
‎| 09 | **Competitors Become Credible Substitutes** | Alternatives no longer feel experimental | Production use cases, not demos | [ ] |
‎| 10 | **Network Effects Weaken** | Incumbent's ecosystem becomes less indispensable | Value of staying decreases | [ ] |
‎| 11 | **Institutional Response Appears** | Pricing, limits, products or policies change | Incumbent reacts to evaluation | [ ] |
‎| 12 | **Narrative Changes** | Yesterday's "Why would anyone leave?" → today's "Everyone uses several." | Media narrative shift | [ ] |
‎| 13 | **Threshold is Crossed** | Individual choices accumulate into structural change | Market share, irreversible migration | [ ] |
‎
‎**Critical Checkpoint:**
‎> **Has evaluation produced behaviour yet?**
‎
‎If No → Observing signal
‎If Yes → Observing migration
‎
‎Until we can answer that with evidence, we're observing a signal, not announcing a migration.
‎
