‎## 3. Historical Control Questions
‎
‎For every present signal, ask:
‎
‎> **Where have we seen this sequence before — and where did the analogy fail?**
‎
‎**Purpose:** Test recurring mechanics, not map one-to-one analogy.
‎
‎**Control Set — Must test against:**
‎
‎| Historical Case | What Crossed | What Failed in Analogy? |
‎| :--- | :--- | :--- |
‎| **Yahoo** | Search → Portal → Search | — |
‎| **Microsoft / Internet Explorer** | Browser dominance → standards shift | — |
‎| **Nokia / Mobile** | Hardware dominance → software platform | — |
‎| **BlackBerry / Smartphones** | Keyboard → touch + app ecosystem | — |
‎| **MySpace / Social Networks** | Early network → stronger network | — |
‎| **Cloud Migration** | On-prem → Cloud | — |
‎| **Other Platform Transitions** | Incumbent → Modular challengers | — |
‎
‎**Rule:** Not because ChatGPT is any of them. Because we're looking for recurring mechanics of a crossroads.
‎
