‎## 5. Connection to Forest Model
‎
‎**From Dispatch 012 + 013:**
‎
‎- Forest changes → friction appears (Stage 01)
‎- Inhabitants evaluate → evaluation headstarts choice (Stage 03)
‎- Quiet experimentation → behaviour precedes declarations (Stage 08)
‎- Migration without announcement → threshold crossed (Stage 13)
‎
‎**Instrument:**
‎> Watch what inhabitants *do* when forest changes — not what they *say* about it.
‎
‎This checklist operationalizes that.
‎
‎**Links to Invariant:**
‎- Choice = Stages 01-03 (evaluation)
‎- Command = Stages 04-05 (experimentation, diversification)
‎- Execution = Stages 06-09 (portability, switching, credible substitutes)
‎- Feedback = Stages 10-11 (network effects, institutional response)
‎- Adaptation → Advance = Stages 12-13 (narrative change, threshold)
